<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>The economic issues and policy in France - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 09:52:57 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>French man charged with rape and murder of schoolgirl Lyhanna</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-french-man-charged-with-rape-murder-of-schoolgirl-lyhanna</link><description>
The main suspect in the death of an 11-year-old girl whose body was found in the Gers region has been charged with the rape and murder of a child. The case has sparked nationwide protests and renewed scrutiny of the French justice system, after it emerged that the suspect had previously been accused of raping another child.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf726d0e-80e3-11f1-9ad7-11c429da1086</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:58:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French parliament passes assisted dying law after years of wrangling</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-france-passes-assisted-dying-law-after-years-of-wrangling</link><description>
France's National Assembly has given its definitive backing to legislation granting terminally ill adults the right to end their lives with medical assistance, bringing to a close a protracted and often fraught political battle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af51b17a-807d-11f1-90a2-95c1f2bcc31e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:10:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg">© REUTERS/Abdul Saboor</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Firefighters tackle flare-ups in Fontainebleau forest after reining in blaze</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260715-firefighters-tackle-flare-ups-in-fontainebleau-forest-after-fires-brought-under-control</link><description>
Around 800 firefighters were still at work in Fontainebleau forest on Wednesday morning, tackling flare-ups after the fires were brought under control the previous day, following 48 hours of intense firefighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f11e2794-802a-11f1-977a-e9047a96864f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 11:45:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg">AFP - FRANCK DESPREZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>European troops and planes join Bastille Day parade in show of unity for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-european-troops-and-warplanes-join-paris-military-bastille-day-parade-in-show-of-unity-for-ukraine</link><description>
Some 500 soldiers from the "Coalition of the Willing" backing Ukraine marched down Paris's Champs-Elysees on ​Tuesday in ‌the annual Bastille Day parade, in a showcase of support for Kyiv and a symbolic flexing of European military muscle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3fa6be6-7f63-11f1-b4bc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C24J99R.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3fa6be6-7f63-11f1-b4bc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C24J99R.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc6904da-7f6b-11f1-a3c5-01014d2074c2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 11:28:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3fa6be6-7f63-11f1-b4bc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C24J99R.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France marks 10 years since Bastille Day terror attack in Nice killed 86</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-france-marks-10-years-since-bastille-day-terror-attack-in-nice-killed-86</link><description>
Religious leaders have gathered in Nice for an interfaith service to pray for the victims of the Bastille Day terror attack, on the eve of the 10th anniversary of the atrocity that killed 86 people and injured more than 400. President Emmanuel Macron is due to lead the main memorial ceremony later on Tuesday, while a minute's silence will be observed before France's World Cup semi-final against Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa8e1a84-7e98-11f1-83f4-efef7f7c984b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:12:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg">AFP - VALERY HACHE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fifty-nine arrested over French wildfires, as Fontainebleau blaze continues</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-france-fifty-nine-arrested-over-wildfires-two-for-fontainebleau-forest-blaze-near-paris</link><description>
A total of 59 people have been arrested across France over suspected deliberate or accidental arson, including two in connection with the wildfire still sweeping through the Fontainebleau forest southeast of Paris, Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez has said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6a01b0a-7f54-11f1-ae18-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T221512Z-683314971-RC29DMA8SHKN-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6a01b0a-7f54-11f1-ae18-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T221512Z-683314971-RC29DMA8SHKN-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11f26780-7f4c-11f1-b471-b182ab756299</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 06:22:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e6a01b0a-7f54-11f1-ae18-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T221512Z-683314971-RC29DMA8SHKN-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">REUTERS - Stephane Mahe</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris balls cancelled amid heatwave as France marks 10 years since Nice attack</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260713-bastille-day-events-disrupted-by-heat-as-france-marks-nice-attack-anniversary</link><description>
Bastille Day firefighters' balls in Paris and the surrounding suburbs have been cancelled owing to record high temperatures affecting the capital and most of France, as emergency workers remain on alert. Celebrations begin on Monday, with Paris having brought forward its annual fireworks display by a day to avoid clashing with commemorations marking the 10th anniversary of the Nice attack of 14 July, 2016.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e326d98-7eb5-11f1-8c6f-fb9125324903</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:25:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Massive fire burns in Fontainebleau near Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260713-massive-fire-burns-in-fontainebleau-near-paris</link><description>
Firefighers are mobilised in the Fontainebleau forest south of Paris to contain a major fire that started Sunday and has since forced the evacuation of residents in the area and shut down a major highway at the start of a busy summer holiday travel weekend.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/91d8dbec-7e83-11f1-bfbe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T210510Z-2118620046-RC2KCMA9N2WS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/91d8dbec-7e83-11f1-bfbe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T210510Z-2118620046-RC2KCMA9N2WS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7d3c358-7e83-11f1-8358-9de93d8b8c57</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:35:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/91d8dbec-7e83-11f1-bfbe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T210510Z-2118620046-RC2KCMA9N2WS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Benoit Tessier/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Champagne, Comté and croissants in the crossfire of climate change</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-champagne-comt%C3%A9-and-croissants-in-the-crossfire-of-climate-change-experts-warn</link><description>
France's June heatwave saw temperatures in Paris hit 41C, the same average as Dubai. Experts now say that, in order to adapt to climate change, the country will have difficult choices to make when it comes to its famed lifestyle. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee0af75e-72b4-11f1-8c42-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/nong-03.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee0af75e-72b4-11f1-8c42-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/nong-03.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e81df1b4-7892-11f1-8ff1-731ac46c8d47</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:52:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee0af75e-72b4-11f1-8c42-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/nong-03.jpg">REUTERS - Tom Nicholson</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France remembers 'old demons' of antisemitism on first annual Dreyfus day</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-france-remembers-old-demons-of-antisemitism-on-first-annual-dreyfus-day</link><description>
Sunday saw France observe its first annual day of commemoration for Alfred Dreyfus, a Jewish army officer wrongly convicted of treason in one of the country's most notorious cases of antisemitism. With reports of hate speech on the rise, President Emmanuel Macron said France had yet to shed its "old demons" of prejudice.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21a8c7dc-7d3a-11f1-84f6-9f5186b7b518</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:44:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e5d9c7be-7dee-11f1-b4bd-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Y88MK.jpg">© AFP - THOMAS SAMSON </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Heatwave forces Tour de France to shorten stage for first time</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260712-heatwave-forces-tour-de-france-to-shorten-stage-for-first-time</link><description>
Tour de France organisers have shortened Sunday's stage by 30km due to extreme heat, the first time in the history of the cycling race that high temperatures have forced a change to the route.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2977ae12-7dd3-11f1-978d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9DV4RN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2977ae12-7dd3-11f1-978d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9DV4RN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a5385368-7dd2-11f1-a47d-5df6a9464878</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:23:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2977ae12-7dd3-11f1-978d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9DV4RN.jpg">© Loic VENANCE / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eiffel Tower, Louvre close early as France faces third heatwave in three months</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260711-eiffel-tower-louvre-close-early-as-france-faces-third-heatwave-in-three-months</link><description>
Three of France's biggest tourist attractions, the Eiffel Tower, the Louvre and the Musée d'Orsay, will close early all weekend as an intense heatwave grips the country for the third time since May. A red alert is in place across Paris and most of north-west France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7827c9b6-6fd2-11f1-a33b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T132434Z-1885014167-RC2SXLAUYP8N-RTRMADP-3-EDF-NUCLEAR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7827c9b6-6fd2-11f1-a33b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T132434Z-1885014167-RC2SXLAUYP8N-RTRMADP-3-EDF-NUCLEAR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6479fc4c-7d27-11f1-8781-d94853d11127</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:52:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7827c9b6-6fd2-11f1-a33b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-24T132434Z-1885014167-RC2SXLAUYP8N-RTRMADP-3-EDF-NUCLEAR.jpg">© REUTERS - Sarah Meyssonnier </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French farmers race to adapt as repeated heatwaves hit crops and livestock</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260711-french-farmers-race-to-adapt-as-repeated-heatwaves-hit-crops-and-livestock</link><description>
After weeks of sweltering heat and drought, farmers and analysts fear France's maize crop could be down by a third this year – making it the smallest in 35 years. Poultry farmers are also counting their losses as many as 3 million broiler chickens died within a few days in in June. The damage is a result of three heatwaves that have already hit France this year, and is only set to intensify as climate change disrupts agriculture across Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/486e780c-7b7e-11f1-a361-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T125055Z-1820761388-RC2N9MA2RTCP-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/486e780c-7b7e-11f1-a361-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T125055Z-1820761388-RC2N9MA2RTCP-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c040005c-7c6a-11f1-ab2f-113e7a8a35f2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 07:04:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/486e780c-7b7e-11f1-a361-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T125055Z-1820761388-RC2N9MA2RTCP-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg">© Benoit Tessier / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Surprise alliance hands anti-independence bloc control of New Caledonia Congress</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260710-surprise-alliance-gives-non-independence-bloc-control-of-new-caledonia-congress</link><description>
The anti-independence bloc has won control of New Caledonia's deliberative assembly, after securing the backing of a small party – despite the two sides holding sharply different views on the future of the French Pacific territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e428373c-7108-11eb-bd31-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9377XF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e428373c-7108-11eb-bd31-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9377XF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e690c908-7c3d-11f1-a622-0b49c900324f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 11:52:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e428373c-7108-11eb-bd31-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9377XF.jpg">AFP - THEO ROUBY</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Bayeux Tapestry delivered to British Museum under cover of darkness</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260710-bayeux-tapestry-arrives-in-britain-in-high-security-night-time-operation</link><description>
After almost 1,000 years, the Bayeux Tapestry is back on English soil – spirited to London's British Museum on Friday in the dead of night, after a high-tech and high-security operation in which any slip-up could have spelled disaster.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/22937990-606f-11f1-9b0d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-Tapestry-scene57-Harold-death.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/22937990-606f-11f1-9b0d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-Tapestry-scene57-Harold-death.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14fa8278-7c27-11f1-96b9-e532d0368fe7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 07:06:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/22937990-606f-11f1-9b0d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Bayeux-Tapestry-scene57-Harold-death.jpg">© Myrabella, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France must speed up climate action, as watchdog warns current efforts fall short</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260710-france-must-speed-up-climate-action-as-watchdog-warns-current-efforts-fall-short</link><description>
France is not prepared for the pace and scale of climate change, the country’s climate watchdog has warned in a report that calls for a significant acceleration of both emission reduction efforts and adaptation policies, as the country faces its third heatwave since May.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33118760-7b9c-11f1-95af-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T064201Z-180942209-RC29ILA7EQ9D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-CLIMATE-ADAPTATION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33118760-7b9c-11f1-95af-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T064201Z-180942209-RC29ILA7EQ9D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-CLIMATE-ADAPTATION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6972d9d6-7b9b-11f1-a938-5b9af79f737d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 05:24:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33118760-7b9c-11f1-95af-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T064201Z-180942209-RC29ILA7EQ9D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-CLIMATE-ADAPTATION.jpg">© Alice Sacco/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Secrecy surrounds Bayeux Tapestry's imminent Channel crossing</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260709-bayeux-tapestry-s-norman-conquest-story-crosses-the-channel-for-the-first-time</link><description>
Under cover of darkness and heavy police guard, the Bayeux Tapestry – a 68-metre embroidered chronicle of the Norman conquest of England, stitched in wool not long after the events it depicts – is set to cross the Channel within days, the official overseeing its move to London has revealed.
